From seedds/nxnative (MIT), task/mesh stage memory from b124b24 (PR #983), with the later
race-free byte-store and zero-count initialization behavior from 1d4b8e82. Uniform immediate
BREV (the upstream ABrev lowering) is admitted only for stage-memory jobs, as OOT mesh shaders need it.
ISBERD and stage output use a shared compute-stage array only when QueryAmpereMeshLayout is set.
Byte stores use the pinned translator's existing SharedStoreSmallIntCas transform and CAS helper;
mark stage-memory instructions as SharedMemory so that transform runs. Drop RZ primitive-count
initialization stores because the wrapper zeroes memory before execution (independent Metal lanes
must not overwrite a later count). Ordinary shaders retain the existing paths and feature flags.

